  "id": "COMPOUND:17465 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Sodium 4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzoate appears to be a target of multiple compounds, including S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, 7-O-Methylmangiferin, and terbutaline, all of which ultimately target the CD276 antigen. This suggests a potential mechanism where these compounds interact with the CD276 antigen through a shared target, MIP, which may act as a bridge in the signaling pathway. The evidence points to a possible role for MIP in mediating the interaction between the compounds and CD276, though the exact nature of this interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same antigen implies a broader therapeutic potential, but further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanisms involved.",
